# POM

## Naming Conventions

- Use `br.com.lsampaioweb` as the `groupId` unless the user requests a different organization namespace.
- Set `<artifactId>` and `<name>` to the same kebab-case identifier.

## Rules

- Set the Spring Boot parent to version `4.1.1`.
- Set the Java version to `25`.
- Set `<version>` to `0.1.0` when the user has not specified a version.
- Declare `<relativePath />` on the `<parent>` block.
- Add only dependencies required by the explicit feature scope.
- Pin a `<version>` on a dependency only when the Spring Boot parent BOM does not manage it.
- Add a `<!-- <one-sentence explanation> -->` comment on the line immediately above every `<dependency>` block.
- Do not add MapStruct, Lombok, or annotation processors unless the user explicitly asks for them.
- Do not add `spring-boot-starter-data-jpa`, `jakarta.persistence`, `hibernate-core`, or any ORM dependency.
- Do not add H2, Derby, or other embedded in-memory databases unless the user explicitly requires an in-memory store.

## Safety Guards

- Never set `<artifactId>` or `<name>` to `demo`, `app`, or `example`.
- Never change the Java version without explicit user approval.
- Never add a milestone, beta, or snapshot version without explicit user approval.
